          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Connecting complex platforms like **MYOB Acumatica (formerly MYOB Advanced)**, **SAP (SAP Business One or S/4HANA)**, **CRMs (Salesforce, Dynamics 365, HubSpot)**, and the **Microsoft 365** ecosystem requires specialists who understand ERP workflows, API architecture (REST/OData), and middleware platforms (e.g., Azure Integration Services, Power Automate, or dedicated iPaaS).\n\nTop system integration specialists based in Adelaide, along with leading national integrators with strong local delivery, provide distinct capabilities across these platforms:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Locally Headquartered in Adelaide\n\n* **Solutions+ (Solutions Plus Partnership)**\n  * **Location:** King William Street, Adelaide.\n  * **Platform Coverage:** **SAP Business One**, **MYOB Acumatica**, and **Microsoft Dynamics 365 / Wiise**.\n  * **Why them:** Solutions+ is uniquely positioned for this combination because they are one of the few Adelaide-headquartered consulting firms that hold official partnerships with both **SAP** and **MYOB**, while also maintaining an active Microsoft practice. They specialize in business process optimization, data flow automation, and integrating ERPs with third-party CRM and reporting tools.\n  * **Best for:** Businesses looking for a local team capable of cross-ERP integration, multi-entity sync, or connecting SAP/MYOB backends with Microsoft 365 applications.\n\n* **COMITS Australia (Commercial IT Solutions)**\n  * **Location:** Prospect, Adelaide.\n  * **Platform Coverage:** **MYOB Acumatica**, custom ERP/CRM integrations, Microsoft environments.\n  * **Why them:** An established Adelaide-based MYOB Enterprise Partner since 2007. They possess in-house enterprise software developers who design custom API connectors and data bridges connecting MYOB Acumatica to front-end CRMs, warehouse tools, and Microsoft 365 workspaces.\n  * **Best for:** Adelaide businesses centered around MYOB Acumatica needing deep local technical support, API development, and CRM tie-ins.\n\n* **Astra Custom Software**\n  * **Location:** Adelaide.\n  * **Platform Coverage:** Bespoke enterprise system integration, API/middleware engineering.\n  * **Why them:** If pre-built software connectors are insufficient and you need custom middleware to mediate data transformations between SAP, MYOB Acumatica, and custom CRM systems, Astra focuses specifically on building reliable integration layers and automated data pipelines.\n  * **Best for:** Custom API development and syncing disparate platforms where no native plug-in exists.\n\n---\n\n### 2. National Integrators with Strong Adelaide & SA Presence\n\n* **Cloud Factory (formerly Inecom)**\n  * **Platform Coverage:** SAP Business One, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central / M365, and MYOB Acumatica.\n  * **Why them:** They are one of Australia’s few multi-platform ERP specialists that actively consult and build integrations across all three major ecosystems: SAP, Microsoft, and Acumatica.\n  * **Best for:** Hybrid environments (e.g., holding companies operating SAP at the parent level and MYOB Acumatica in subsidiaries, connected via Microsoft 365).\n\n* **Leverage Technologies**\n  * **Platform Coverage:** SAP Business One, MYOB Acumatica, Sage, Microsoft Power Platform.\n  * **Why them:** Although based nationally, Leverage regularly services the South Australian market. They have an established development wing specialized in ERP customization, API bridging, and connecting core financial backends into CRM/M365 tools.\n  * **Best for:** Complex data migration, bi-directional sync between SAP/Acumatica, and robust enterprise workflows.\n\n* **MyIntegrator / SAAS Integrator**\n  * **Platform Coverage:** Cloud ERPs (SAP B1, MYOB Acumatica, NetSuite) to CRMs (HubSpot, Salesforce, Dynamics).\n  * **Why them:** Specialists in iPaaS (Integration Platform as a Service) architectures. Rather than writing code from scratch, they supply pre-tested connectors configured for continuous, real-time data sync across inventory, customer records, and orders.\n  * **Best for:** Fast deployment of standard bi-directional data synchronization between CRM and ERP systems.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps for Selection\n\n1. **Map Your Architecture Pattern:**\n   * If using **Microsoft 365 / Teams / Power BI** as your operational hub, ensure the integrator has certified **Azure / Power Platform** expertise so integrations leverage native event triggers (Power Automate, Azure Service Bus).\n   * If connecting **SAP** and **MYOB Acumatica** simultaneously (e.g., dual-ERP setup or post-merger integration), shortlist **Solutions+** or **Cloud Factory**, as they hold direct partner accreditations in both systems.\n2. **Review API Limits:** Both SAP Business One (Service Layer) and MYOB Acumatica have distinct API rate limits and data models; request examples from the partner showing how they handle asynchronous batching and queue management to avoid performance bottlenecks.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
